vided by RefSeq, Jul 2013].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q6P5W5","text":"Selective transporter that mediates the uptake of Zn(2+) (PubMed:17202136, PubMed:22242765, PubMed:27321477, PubMed:28875161, PubMed:31164399, PubMed:31914589, PubMed:31979155, PubMed:33837739, PubMed:36473915). Plays an essential role for dietary zinc uptake from small intestine (By similarity). The Zn(2+) uniporter activity is regulated by zinc availability (PubMed:17202136, PubMed:32348750). Also exhibits polyspecific binding and transport of Cu(2+), Cd(2+) and possibly Ni(2+) but at higher concentrations (PubMed:22242765, PubMed:31914589)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}